### first 240 KB attempt: harness did not retransmit a lost tail
    assert ok and predicate(), f'timed out waiting for {what}'
           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
AssertionError: timed out waiting for upload ACK
It stalled at 8,222,560 of 8,388,608 bytes with input_fail=115 and up_phase=lwip_recv.
After the sender learned to go-back-N the unacknowledged tail, the same config
finished with zero netd drops, so the earlier failure must not be read as a
queue limit. Over-driving (about 20k segments/s here) remains the real trigger.

